Week 2 — r2pipe Hooking (with a stand-in process for now)

Step 1 — Install Radare2:

bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y radare2

Verify it installed:

bash
r2 -v

Step 2 — Install r2pipe (Radare2's Python API), inside your venv:

bash
source firmsight-env/bin/activate
pip install r2pipe

Step 3 — Create a simple long-running "stand-in" process to attach to (this represents where your real emulated firmware process will run later — for now, just something alive long enough to inspect):

bash
nano dummy_process.c

Compile and run it in the background:

bash
gcc -o dummy_process dummy_process.c
./dummy_process &

Note the PID it prints when backgrounded (or run pgrep dummy_process to find it).

Step 4 — Write the r2pipe script that attaches to it and dumps memory maps:

bash
nano r2_hook.py

Step 5 — Run it (needs sudo since attaching to another process requires ptrace permissions):

bash
sudo python3 r2_hook.py

Good — Radare2 installed cleanly (version 6.0.7). Now let's continue with the rest of Week 2.

